Watch files and re-run a task on changes

Usage: mk watch [OPTIONS] [TASK_NAME] [-- <TRAILING_ARGS>...]

Arguments:
  [TASK_NAME]         The task name to run
  [TRAILING_ARGS]...  Arguments forwarded to the task on each run (available as ${{ args.0 }}, ${{ args.1 }}, etc.)

Options:
      --label <FILTER>       Watch tasks matching label (KEY or KEY=VALUE). Repeatable; all must match.
      --path <PATH>          Override watched paths (repeatable; defaults to task inputs when absent)
      --debounce <DURATION>  Debounce duration for filesystem event coalescing (e.g. 500ms, 1s, 2.5s)
      --clear                Clear terminal before each rerun (default: append output)
  -h, --help                 Print help
  -V, --version              Print version
